<h2>Nederland and Port Arthur</h2>
<p>Nederland is only a short drive from Port Arthur, and the two cities share the same county government, the same NWS forecast office in Lake Charles, the same weather station at Jack Brooks Regional Airport, and the same TWIA status. A storm that damages Port Arthur roofs very often damages Nederland roofs the same night. As a Port Arthur Public Adjuster serving all of Mid-County, we bring the same inspection, documentation, and policy review process to Nederland claims that we use throughout Jefferson County.</p>

<h2>When to get help</h2>
<p>You do not need a public adjuster for every claim. It may be worth a conversation if your claim was <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied</a> or <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid</a>, you have separate TWIA and flood claims for the same storm, the insurer's estimate does not match what your contractor says the repair requires, or the claim has stalled. Request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> and we will give you an honest assessment. Coverage always depends on your policy and the facts of the loss.</p>
